  "term": "recognition",
  "definition": "In this source, recognition means establishing that a collective experience has occurred by identifying a shared relational pattern rather than relying on any one person’s private report. It depends on the group reaching coordinated alignment in action, perception, and intention, so that the experience becomes recognizable as a collective event.",
